    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="25617d7b-22b9-5aff-b0b7-eaf98791d4ae" activityNameId="b9ab2a1b-6151-5918-b2b1-685fcbe37a2d" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Window frame, wood, w/o surface treatment, m2 visible, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Window frame, wood, w/o surface treatment, m2 visible, at plant
The measures of the window are 1.75m (width) x 1.3m (height). The average visible area is 0.29m2. 1m2 of visible wooden window frame weighs 122.8kg. The bill of materials is based on data from 3 window producers.;
UUID: f0ef9255-921a-3adc-9782-773d9c62ab18
Included are the materials used in a wooden window frame (without surface treatment). Production losses, work materials, packaging materials, energy demand and the transport of the materials are also included.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Industry data.
Time period: Time of publications.
Production volume: na
Sampling: Data survey at 4 window manufacturers in Switzerland. 
Extrapolations: Some generic datasets from ecoinvent have been used.
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_f0ef9255-921a-3adc-9782-773d9c62ab18.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
